    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0586" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d320-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-21">December 21, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President for the Former Naval Person personal and secret No. 242.</p>
                <p>Following is the substance of letter<anchor n="2" xml:id="d320-f2"/> which
                    courier has for you: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In spite of Stalin’s inability to meet with us I think we should plan a
                            meeting at once with our respective military staffs. I should like to
                            meet in Africa about January 15th. There is I believe a satisfactory and
                            safe place just north of Casablanca. It might be wise for some of our
                            military men to precede us by a few days to clear the ground. I should
                            think if we could have four or five days together we could clear up all
                            of our business.</p>
                        <p>“Will you let me know what you think of this.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d320-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d320-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d320-f2" n="2" xml:id="d320-f2-content">
                <p>The reference is to Roosevelt’s letter of December 11, 1942, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg498">p. 498</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
